dont-run-from-the-cops/93248","site":"T Nation · 136 posts · 2007"},{"title":"Premier of Rogue Vampire's Book!","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/premier-of-rogue-vampires-book/176721","site":"T Nation · 105 posts · 2012"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Flight jackets — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Flight_jacket"},{"title":"Flight jacket","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flight_jacket"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Fat loss","chain":["Waist-length cut with ribbed hem","Defined waist and structured shoulder line","Balanced, athletic-looking outline","Classic masculine outfit"],"effect":"direct","text":"The short cut and elastic hem emphasise the waist and shoulders, so the jacket works as a layering piece that frames the upper body."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Flight_jacket","lead":["A flight jacket, also called a bomber or aviator jacket, is a short outer garment developed for pilots flying in cold, open or unheated aircraft.[1][2]","The U.S. Army's Aviation Clothing Board began issuing heavy leather flight jackets in September 1917. The A-2 followed in 1931, the Navy's G-1 paralleled it, the B-3 became the Air Force shearling bomber, and the nylon MA-1, usually sage green with a blaze orange lining, is the model most people now associate with the term.[1]","Civilians adopted the style through scooterboy and skinhead subcultures, 1980s baseball-style bombers and early-2000s hip-hop fashion, and Raf Simons brought the MA-1 into high fashion in 2001, per Wikipedia.[1] For looks, the cropped length and snug cuffs shape the waist and shoulders."],"infobox":[["Type","Outerwear"],["Origin","Military aviation, c. 1910s-1930s"],["Notable models","A-2, G-1, B-3, MA-1"],["Materials","Leather, shearling, nylon"],["Distinctive features","Ribbed cuffs and waistband, zip front"]],"sections":[{"h":"Design and types","paras":["Classic features are a waist-length body, knit cuffs and hem, and a front zip. Leather versions use horsehide or goatskin, shearling versions add warmth, and the MA-1 uses nylon with an orange lining.[1][2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Early pilots wore heavy coats against wind and cold; the Aviation Clothing Board was established in 1917 and set standards for leather flight jackets.[1] The jacket moved into mainstream wear through subcultures and fashion houses, and Top Gun reportedly raised G-1 sales.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1917","event":"U.S. Army Aviation Clothing Board begins issuing leather flight jackets.[1]"},{"year":"1931","event":"A-2 jacket introduced for Army Air Corps pilots.[1]"},{"year":"2001","event":"Raf Simons shows the MA-1 in a high-fashion collection.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Flight jacket","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flight_jacket","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Flight jacket","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Flight_jacket","source":"Grokipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Dani's Rebel Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/danis-rebel-log/280747","site":"T Nation · 3979 posts · 2023"},{"title":"WannaBe’s Last Year Of “DYEL?”","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/wannabe-s-last-year-of-dyel/268239","site":"T Nation · 2227 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Yogi's Random Training Thoughts","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/yogis-random-training-thoughts/221798","site":"T Nation · 1549 posts · 2016"},{"title":"Black Teen Shot 3","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/black-teen-shot-3/176620","site":"T Nation · 1126 posts · 2012"},{"title":"KMC's Blackirish Bastid Kicks Ass 2.0","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/kmcs-blackirish-bastid-kicks-ass-2-0/139770","site":"T Nation · 675 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Dude, You are Swole","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/dude-you-are-swole/146040","site":"T Nation · 547 posts · 2010"}]}